From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hans2294 <22217531+hans2294@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:09:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libsync.h: Linux's ioctl encoding on Haiku

radeonsi's DRI frontend uses Mesa's copy of libsync.h; like libdrm's, it
takes _IOWR() from the sys/ioccom.h libdrm installs for linuxkpi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/util/libsync.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/util/libsync.h b/src/util/libsync.h
index b22b75a..d412cf2 100644
--- a/src/util/libsync.h
+++ b/src/util/libsync.h
@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/ioctl.h>
+#ifdef __HAIKU__
+#include <sys/ioccom.h>	/* Linux's _IOWR() for linuxkpi, from libdrm */
+#endif
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <time.h>
